      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/zazzcode/zazzles",
          "name": "scan",
          "rules": [
            {
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Protect the specific browser rendering context\n\n- Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.\n- Use escaped template output for HTML text and quoted non-active attributes; use textContent for plain DOM text.\n- For intentional rich HTML, apply a verified maintained sanitizer before every sink; inspect its configuration and version.\n- Treat script, URL, event-handler and unquoted-attribute contexts separately. HTML entity encoding alone does not protect them.\n- Preserve source, storage and output links when fixing reflected or stored flows; test the protected counterpart.\n",
                "text": "Protect the specific browser rendering context. Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change. Use escaped template output for HTML text and quoted non-active attributes; use textContent for plain DOM text. For intentional rich HTML, apply a verified maintained sanitizer before every sink; inspect its configuration and version. Treat script, URL, event-handler and unquoted-attribute contexts separately. HTML entity encoding alone does not protect them. Preserve source, storage and output links when fixing reflected or stored flows; test the protected counterpart."
              },
              "id": "scan/xss-output-protection",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-79"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Protect the specific browser rendering context"
              }
            },
            {
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Validate and sanitize each request input\n\n- Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.\n- Define the server-side field policy, then enforce applicable type, presence, length, range, and format constraints before use. Free text must remain valid for its business purpose.\n- Use destination-specific protection independently of field validation: SQL parameter binding or a verified NoSQL document API with constrained keys and scalar types. Do not apply a generic sanitizer as a substitute.\n- Preserve an explicit Inconclusive result when a call receives the field but its effect has not been established.\n",
                "text": "Validate and sanitize each request input. Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change. Define the server-side field policy, then enforce applicable type, presence, length, range, and format constraints before use. Free text must remain valid for its business purpose. Use destination-specific protection independently of field validation: SQL parameter binding or a verified NoSQL document API with constrained keys and scalar types. Do not apply a generic sanitizer as a substitute. Preserve an explicit Inconclusive result when a call receives the field but its effect has not been established."
              },
              "id": "scan/input-validation",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-20"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Validate and sanitize each request input"
              }
            },
            {
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Keep request data out of NoSQL query structure\n\n- Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.\n- Reject objects and operators in fields that should be scalars before they reach a query, update, or insert document.\n- Do not concatenate or interpolate request values into $where strings.\n- Inspect numeric conversions and character filters on each actual path before judging their effect. Prefer data-only query APIs over executable $where strings.\n",
                "text": "Keep request data out of NoSQL query structure. Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change. Reject objects and operators in fields that should be scalars before they reach a query, update, or insert document. Do not concatenate or interpolate request values into $where strings. Inspect numeric conversions and character filters on each actual path before judging their effect. Prefer data-only query APIs over executable $where strings."
              },
              "id": "scan/nosql-input-protection",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-943"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Keep request data out of NoSQL query structure"
              }
            },
            {
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Keep credential and personal-data content out of logs\n\n- Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.\n- Remove the value from the log entry, or log a non-revealing fact (presence, length, match result, or a non-reversible identifier) instead.\n- Log an allowlist of fields rather than whole request bodies, queries, or header sets. Never log Authorization or Cookie header values.\n- If redaction is required, apply a verified redaction before the logger call or in the logger's configuration, and test that emitted lines no longer contain the value.\n- Do not send credentials in URL query strings; access logs, proxies, and browser history record URLs. Use a request body or header instead.\n\nIllustrative example (unverified):\n\n```typescript\n// Illustrative: log a fact about the credential, not the credential.\nconsole.info('login attempt', { username, passwordProvided: typeof password === 'string' \u0026\u0026 password.length \u003e 0 });\n```\n",
                "text": "Keep credential and personal-data content out of logs. Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change. Remove the value from the log entry, or log a non-revealing fact (presence, length, match result, or a non-reversible identifier) instead. Log an allowlist of fields rather than whole request bodies, queries, or header sets. Never log Authorization or Cookie header values. If redaction is required, apply a verified redaction before the logger call or in the logger's configuration, and test that emitted lines no longer contain the value. Do not send credentials in URL query strings; access logs, proxies, and browser history record URLs. Use a request body or header instead."
              },
              "id": "scan/sensitive-data-logging",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-532"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Keep credential and personal-data content out of logs"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
